=0.02E(t),$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since the year $2017.$ In $2021,$ the average monthly cost was $$124.50.$ What was the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017?$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326150 1113 #uuid "d1d42a16-3984-5dae-bf8b-539545f414f5" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326150 1145 "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nE(t)={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${E}_{0}$ is the average monthly cost of electricity in $2017.$\n\nWe are given that the monthly residential electricity cost was $$124.50$ in $2021,$ so after $t=4$ years. Hence, substituting $t=4$ and $E(4)=124.50$ into our general solution and solving for ${E}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(4) & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.02\\cdot 4} \\\\ 124.50 & ={E}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08} \\\\ {E}_{0} & =\\frac{124.50}{{e}^{0.08}} \\\\  & ≈114.93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest cent.\n\nTherefore, the average monthly cost in $2017$ was $$114.93.$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326152 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326153 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326154 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326155 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326156 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326156 13194139535004 true] [17592186326151 1110 #uuid "bd14324e-4b95-551f-bc7a-3003dd9bbfe2" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326152 1034 "$$31.13$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326152 1111 #uuid "921b5e26-ac50-5182-b803-8acf97d7c381" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326153 1034 "$$116.01$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326153 1111 #uuid "9c248927-cf87-5799-a64a-2af0d4b12e4d" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326154 1034 "$$122.03$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326154 1111 #uuid "196b8bc5-f372-5676-a6e7-e98af420b532" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326155 1034 "$$113.25$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326155 1111 #uuid "add65ded-36d4-522b-8ca0-ebf3ee64d7c8" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326156 1034 "$$114.93$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326156 1111 #uuid "a850e578-cba5-5daf-9d0e-c47606e88b88" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326158 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1089 "q-340560" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1100 "The rate at which the price of a particular product changes $P(t),$ after $t$ years, is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.042P.\n$$\n\nIf the price today is $$120,$ how many years will it take for the price to increase to $$750?$\nRound your answer to the nearest year." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1113 #uuid "982ed208-e355-5a90-b941-1b6ff05c7454" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326157 1145 "We model the price growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=0.042P.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.042t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that the price today is $$120,$ so we have ${P}_{0}=120.$\n\nTherefore, the price $P$ of the product after $t$ years is\n\n$$\nP(t)=120\\,{e}^{0.042t}\\,.\n$$\n\nTo find how many years it takes for the price to grow to $$750,$ we substitute $P(t)=750$ into the equation above and solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}750 & =120\\,{e}^{0.042t} \\\\ \\frac{750}{120} & ={e}^{0.042t} \\\\ {e}^{0.042t} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.042t}) & =ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ 0.042t & =ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{0.042}ln\\,(\\frac{25}{4}) \\\\ t & ≈43.633\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $44$ years for the price to increase to $$750.$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326159 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326160 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326161 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326162 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326163 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326162 13194139535004 true] [17592186326158 1110 #uuid "fb94e7a9-c401-5f27-81f2-530a753139e8" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326159 1034 "38" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535004 true] [17592186326159 1111 #uuid "99c619a9-f8e7-5ced-adbd-7bd2d24ba835" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326160 1034 "47" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535004 true] [17592186326160 1111 #uuid "f56e05ce-e2ee-53cf-936a-614ecb385f65" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326161 1034 "41" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535004 true] [17592186326161 1111 #uuid "b97c1c1b-4d13-5cfc-97da-e6f6340889b0" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326162 1034 "44" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535004 true] [17592186326162 1111 #uuid "3b4bf58c-1734-503d-bc33-9204c8c95d1a" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326163 1034 "52" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535004 true] [17592186326163 1111 #uuid "3f492ca8-ea13-59d0-8320-2e74ecc15f19" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326165 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1089 "q-340589" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1100 "The rate at which the population of yeast cells in a laboratory culture grows $Y(t),$ after $t$ days, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}Y}{\\text{d}t}=0.55Y.\n$$\n\nHow many days does it take for the population to triple? Round your answer to the nearest day." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1113 #uuid "5f6bdeb7-1079-54d3-b26a-5b089c222d68" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326164 1145 "We model the population growth using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}Y}{\\text{d}t}=0.55Y.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nY(t)={Y}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.55t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Y}_{0}$ is the initial population.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the population is triple the initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nY({t}_{1})=3{Y}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y({t}_{1}) & ={Y}_{0}{e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3{Y}_{0} & ={Y}_{0}{e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3 & ={e}^{0.55{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.55{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =0.55{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{0.55} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈1.997\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $2$ days for the population to triple." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326166 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326167 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326168 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326169 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326170 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326168 13194139535004 true] [17592186326165 1110 #uuid "1407b21c-3593-5bf9-b78a-74ff78175b10" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326166 1034 "$6$ days" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326166 1111 #uuid "204d3fac-aaf8-55c8-bec6-c76e2300150c" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326167 1034 "$3$ days" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326167 1111 #uuid "3a84082f-c4b4-570d-9b66-a621cf326595" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326168 1034 "$2$ days" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326168 1111 #uuid "54881899-a54c-5639-b946-26bf0330b188" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326169 1034 "$8$ days" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326169 1111 #uuid "69d6973f-b2aa-50a2-b0cd-c3507f337e57" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326170 1034 "$9$ days" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326170 1111 #uuid "a3228e04-03c5-5a44-bed9-74f7f5973017" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326172 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1089 "q-340590" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1100 "The rate at which the number of independent mobile applications on a digital marketplace grows $A(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.35A.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the number of applications to triple? Round your answer to the nearest year." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1113 #uuid "650d5288-3ff5-5a26-b0f1-c9e721ddc977" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326171 1145 "We model the growth in the number of applications using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.35A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.35t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial number of applications.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of applications is triple the initial number. That is,\n\n$$\nA({t}_{1})=3{A}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A({t}_{1}) & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3{A}_{0} & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ 3 & ={e}^{0.35{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.35{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =0.35{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{0.35} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈3.139\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $3$ years for the number of applications to triple." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326173 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326174 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326175 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326176 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326177 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326175 13194139535004 true] [17592186326172 1110 #uuid "b57d4f66-d561-5057-b00e-13d0a49edace" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326173 1034 "$6$ years" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326173 1111 #uuid "3dab4e65-2954-51d0-970d-3cb9f9814b56" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326174 1034 "$4$ years" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326174 1111 #uuid "b904d403-ada7-5a0e-adda-aef9ed57399f" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326175 1034 "$3$ years" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326175 1111 #uuid "19af726d-92f9-5c81-9c19-2443ae32a2f3" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326176 1034 "$2$ years" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326176 1111 #uuid "ce56bc40-31e3-536a-8287-7f9ed0025523" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326177 1034 "$5$ years" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326177 1111 #uuid "b53f21dd-3f1b-5fed-afd2-52caa8ef4f31" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326179 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1089 "q-340627" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1100 "The rate at which the cultivated area of a particular region grows $A(t),$ after $t$ years, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.08A.\n$$\n\nHow many years does it take for the cultivated area to increase by $40%?$ Round your answer to the nearest decimal place." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1113 #uuid "7cff2abe-4fb8-5bec-8737-031cabfdd6ec" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326178 1145 "We model the growth of the cultivated area using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.08A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial cultivated area.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the cultivated area has increased by $40%.$ That is,\n\n$$\nA({t}_{1})=1.4{A}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A({t}_{1}) & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08\\cdot {t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4{A}_{0} & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4 & ={e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{0.08{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4) & =0.08{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.4)}{0.08} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈4.205\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest decimal place, we conclude that it takes $4.2$ years for the cultivated area to increase by $40%.$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326180 13194139535004 true] [17592186326179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326181 13194139535004 true] [17592186326179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326182 13194139535004 true] [175921863