rocessed records to decrease to $1\\,000?$ Round your answer to the nearest minute." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326185 1113 #uuid "f2af16ce-2cfd-5b65-bea9-d42294a55eb0" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326185 1145 "We model the number of unprocessed records using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}t}=-0.25R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nR(t)={R}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.25t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${R}_{0}$ is the initial number of unprocessed records.\n\nWe're told that there are $20\\,000$ unprocessed records at the start of the scan, so we have ${R}_{0}=20\\,000.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of unprocessed records has decreased to $1\\,000.$ That is,\n\n$$\nR({t}_{1})=1\\,000.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,000 & =20\\,000{e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{1\\,000}{20\\,000} & ={e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.05 & ={e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.25{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05) & =-0.25{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.05)}{-0.25} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈11.982\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $12$ minutes for the number of unprocessed records to decrease to $1\\,000.$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326187 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326188 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326189 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326190 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326191 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326187 13194139535004 true] [17592186326186 1110 #uuid "088006b6-6f61-5dce-900e-d7da50500335" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326187 1034 "$12$ minutes" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326187 1111 #uuid "e586fdc9-4857-5510-ab6a-7af970785f02" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326188 1034 "$15$ minutes" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326188 1111 #uuid "7134a2bd-5e23-50cf-a75c-eb9627ff681a" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326189 1034 "$8$ minutes" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326189 1111 #uuid "7af6d728-8e07-5da8-b552-3f7ac548f63d" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326190 1034 "$6$ minutes" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326190 1111 #uuid "f5846e49-a3f8-5c48-a2b6-d956ab8e10ec" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326191 1034 "$20$ minutes" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326191 1111 #uuid "37b67c09-2b58-5660-91dd-4eed3018c1d9" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326193 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1089 "q-340695" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1100 "The rate at which the number of active users of a mobile app decreases $U(t),$ after $t$ weeks from launch, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}U}{\\text{d}t}=-0.04U.\n$$\n\nIf there are $40\\,000$ active users at launch, how many weeks does it take for the number of active users to decrease to $20\\,000?$  Round your answer to the nearest week." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1113 #uuid "b9919d3f-10c9-53e2-8d3a-e92839556535" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326192 1145 "We model the number of active users using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}U}{\\text{d}t}=-0.04U.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nU(t)={U}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.04t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${U}_{0}$ is the initial number of active users.\n\nWe're told that there are $40\\,000$ active users at launch, so we have ${U}_{0}=40\\,000.$\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the number of active users has decreased to $20\\,000.$ That is,\n\n$$\nU({t}_{1})=20\\,000.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20\\,000 & =40\\,000{e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{20\\,000}{40\\,000} & ={e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.5 & ={e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.04{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5) & =-0.04{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.5)}{-0.04} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈17.329\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest integer, we conclude that it takes $17$ weeks for the number of active users to decrease to $20\\,000.$" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326194 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326195 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326196 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326197 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326198 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326194 13194139535004 true] [17592186326193 1110 #uuid "da4ccf10-1528-51c9-832a-f68749c13838" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326194 1034 "$17$ weeks" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326194 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326194 1111 #uuid "c824b699-e8fb-5750-920d-e6ba929a6292" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326195 1034 "$20$ weeks" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326195 1111 #uuid "19126342-60d5-5541-9058-1d89b8a1546c" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326196 1034 "$8$ weeks" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326196 1111 #uuid "3452282a-4e4e-55cc-a748-23bfd64cce7b" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326197 1034 "$25$ weeks" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326197 1111 #uuid "868cbb1a-4f0b-50fe-a68e-b4192e1f8db3" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326198 1034 "$12$ weeks" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326198 1111 #uuid "4d8f8d56-e5ed-5630-97be-5d4b2ee23df2" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326200 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1089 "q-340837" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1100 "A balloon is being deflated. The rate at which the diameter of the balloon decays $D(t),$ after $t$ seconds, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-0.20D.\n$$\n\nHow long does it take for the balloon’s diameter to reduce to $15%$ of its original diameter?  Round your answer to the nearest second." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1113 #uuid "810a12d9-d044-5bce-b3d6-cf6256a5234a" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326199 1145 "We model the diameter of the balloon using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-0.20D.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nD(t)={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.20t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${D}_{0}$ is the initial diameter.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the diameter of the balloon is $15%$ of its original diameter. That is,\n\n$$\nD({t}_{1})=0.15{D}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.15{D}_{0} & ={D}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.15 & ={e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.20{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15) & =-0.20{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.15)}{0.20} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈9.486\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest second, we conclude that it takes $9$ seconds for the balloon’s diameter to be $15%$ of its original diameter." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326201 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326202 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326203 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326204 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326205 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326201 13194139535004 true] [17592186326200 1110 #uuid "028480f5-0141-5235-8aca-ae2535c9ecc4" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326201 1034 "$9$ seconds" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326201 1111 #uuid "05e03ecf-05b0-5600-b527-c2a42c1e1ae6" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326202 1034 "$5$ seconds" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326202 1111 #uuid "92d0fac6-046f-5227-9ef8-9dd30d5a88c5" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326203 1034 "$15$ seconds" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326203 1111 #uuid "10a7fda7-2e7c-5a97-b4ec-b4ea1282cc78" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326204 1034 "$7$ seconds" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326204 1111 #uuid "8b914939-e315-5671-9a86-96c5c6509dbf" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326205 1034 "$12$ seconds" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] [17592186326205 1111 #uuid "199fe34b-d8c1-5974-a53f-002c3b369a47" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326207 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1089 "q-340839" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1100 "The amount of charge stored in a battery is decreasing due to self-discharge. The rate at which the amount of stored charge decays $W(t),$ after $t$ months, can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.025W.\n$$\n\nHow long does it take for the amount of stored charge to be $75%$ of the original amount? Round your answer to the nearest month." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1113 #uuid "e95d42fb-17c7-5032-aeb8-e1c39a0b2c28" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326206 1145 "We model the amount of stored charge using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-0.025W.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nW(t)={W}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.025t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${W}_{0}$ is the initial stored charge.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the amount of stored charge is $75%$ of the original amount. That is,\n\n$$\nW({t}_{1})=0.75{W}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.75{W}_{0} & ={W}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}} \\\\ 0.75 & ={e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-0.025{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75) & =-0.025{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.75)}{0.025} \\\\ {t}_{1} & ≈11.507\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest month, we conclude that it takes $12$ months for the amount of stored charge to be $75%$ of the original amount." 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326208 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326209 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326210 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326211 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326212 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1041 "selection" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326212 13194139535004 true] [17592186326207 1110 #uuid "e1ee6832-3fd9-5359-bbf2-55128a903aa0" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326208 1034 "$6$ months" 13194139535004 true] [17592186326208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535004 true] 